  "responseTimeMs": 19803,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA VAT-registered exporter that sells 100% of its goods abroad can obtain a refund or tax credit for input VAT. This is provided under the provisions of the NIRC.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor VAT-registered exporters, this provision is significant as it allows them to effectively reduce their tax burden by recovering input VAT. This can enhance cash flow and competitiveness in the international market, as exporters can reclaim VAT that would otherwise be a cost to their operations. It is essential for exporters to maintain proper documentation and comply with the filing requirements to successfully claim these refunds or credits.",
